<!--
    Region-based (Phoenix/SAILR) structurer, Increment 1 PoC  -  option
    `regionstructure` (default OFF).  This proves the structuring seam end to end:
    under `option regionstructure on`, `ActionBlockStructure` replaces Ghidra's
    `CollapseStructure` with the region-driven structurer
    (`s8_structure::region_structurer`), which runs the KunaRegionIdentifier over
    the real CFG (the W7 `build_from_block_graph` adapter) and structures the
    seeded `sblocks` graph with the acyclic-sequence schema + structural-ITE
    schema + the SAILR-ordered virtualize-to-goto fallback.

    `proof_fn` is the canonical `if(c){A}else{B} -> join -> tail` shape (x86-64,
    GCC -O0, the bytes [0x401106, 0x401152) of a linked no-PIE executable; the
    one global `g` lives at 0x40402c).  Source:

        volatile int g;
        int proof_fn(int c, int x) {
            int r;
            if (c) { r = x + 1; g =  r; }   // A (then)
            else   { r = x - 1; g = -r; }   // B (else)
            r = r * 2;                       // join (sequence after the if/else)
            return r + g;                    // tail
        }

    The region structurer folds this with its acyclic-sequence schema (the
    join->tail run) + the structural-ITE schema (the if/else diamond), producing
    a goto-free `if (c) {...} else {...} return ...;`  -  verified to take the
    structurer's success path (not the CollapseStructure fall-back).

    Parity proof: the region-driven structuring is byte-identical to Ghidra's
    `CollapseStructure` on this acyclic shape, so pass 1 (off) and pass 2 (on)
    emit the SAME C  -  both ZERO gotos.  This is the honest Inc 1 result: Ghidra's
    acyclic structurer is already complete (sequence/if/if-else/short-circuit), so
    the region structurer MATCHES it on acyclic code rather than beating it.  The
    goto-count reduction the roadmap targets lives in the cyclic increments
    (loops/break-continue, Inc 3)  -  see docs/region-structurer-roadmap.md and the
    Inc 1 analysis in the PR; Inc 1 delivers the parity-safe foundation + the
    live, correct sequence/ITE/virtualize seam.

    Stage model: S8 "structuring" / goto-quality.  `option regionstructure off`
    (default) is byte-identical to the existing pipeline; `on` swaps in the
    region structurer.  Asserted invariants below hold across BOTH passes (so the
    counts are 2x the per-pass count): the structured if/else body, the join
    sequence, the tail return, and ZERO gotos.
-->
